=bl&ots=3-rirDOY9S&sig=ACfU3U2SXiNDAkXcLsQG-VAchhIu6H2z-A&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwiqwd2xy_6EAxVJCTQIHX2kBrg4ChDoAXoECAIQAw#v=onepage&q=sarume%20miko&f=false|title=The Japanese Theatre: From Shamanistic Ritual to Contemporary Pluralism|last=Ortolani|first=Benito|date=1995|publisher=Princeton University Press|isbn=978-0-691-04333-3|language=en}}</ref>

There is a Sarume shrine which is a subshrine of [[Sarutahiko Shrine]] dedicated to them.<ref name=":0">https://en.ise-kanko.jp/purpose/sarutahikojinja/</ref><ref name=":1">https://en.ise-kanko.jp/purpose/sarumejinja/</ref><ref name=":2">https://www.sarutahikojinja.or.jp/english/</ref><ref name=":3">https://www.kankomie.or.jp/report/1556?wovn=en#02</ref>

