Later in their history they are said to have interbred with the {{ill|Wani clan|en||simple}}<ref>{{Cite journal|last=Akima|first=Toshio|date=1993|title=The Origins of the Grand Shrine of Ise and the Cult of the Sun Goddess Amaterasu Ōmikami|url=https://www.jstor.org/stable/25790929|journal=Japan Review|issue=4|pages=141–198|issn=0915-0986}}</ref> Which is believed to be related to {{ill|Wani (dragon)|lt=Wani dragons|en||simple}}, with Naniwa-neko Takefurukuma described as an ancestor. Marrying women of the Wani clan was believed to give the Emperor control over the sea.<ref name="Akima-1993a">{{Cite journal|last=Akima|first=Toshio|date=1993|title=The Origins of the Grand Shrine of Ise and the Cult of the Sun Goddess Amaterasu Ōmikami|url=https://www.jstor.org/stable/25790929|journal=Japan Review|issue=4|pages=141–198|issn=0915-0986}}</ref>{{Rp|page=149-150}} The wani clan had a similar religious role to the {{ill|Sarume clan|lt=Sarume clan|simple|User:Immanuelle/Sarume clan|en:draft|6=ja|7=猿女君|8=fr|9=Clan Sarume}} as mediums, so many women of the {{ill|Sarume clan|lt=Sarume clan|simple|User:Immanuelle/Sarume clan|en:draft|6=ja|7=猿女君|8=fr|9=Clan Sarume}} had husbands of the Wani clan perform ritual roles as substitutes for men of the {{ill|Sarume clan|lt=Sarume clan|simple|User:Immanuelle/Sarume clan|en:draft|6=ja|7=猿女君|8=fr|9=Clan Sarume}}.<ref name="Akima-1993a" />{{Rp|page=168}} Their female dancers did many dances that eventually seemed to fuse with the ceremonies of the Miko. Later on records of the Sarume disappeared.<ref name="Ortolani-1995" />

[[Sarutahiko Shrine|Sarutahiko Shrine]] in Ise is linked to the same founding myth. The priests of the shrine are said to also be descendants of {{ill|Sarutahiko Ōkami|en||simple|User:Immanuelle/Sarutahiko Ōkami|6=fr}}.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Dedicated to Sarutahiko Okami, the Kami of Guidance｜みちひらきの大神 猿田彦神社|url=https://www.sarutahikojinja.or.jp/english/|access-date=2023-10-21|website=www.sarutahikojinja.or.jp}}</ref> who it worships.<ref>{{Cite web|date=2022-01-22|title=Sarutahiko {{!}} 國學院大學デジタルミュージアム|url=https://d-museum.kokugakuin.ac.jp/eos/detail/?id=9158|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220122143817/https://d-museum.kokugakuin.ac.jp/eos/detail/?id=9158|archive-date=2022-01-22|access-date=2023-12-07}}</ref>

There is a Sarume shrine which is a subshrine of [[Sarutahiko Shrine|Sarutahiko Shrine]] dedicated to them.<ref name="web.archive.org-2023a" /><ref name="web.archive.org-2022" /><ref name="web.archive.org-2023b" /><ref name="www.kankomie.or.jp" />

